From fb234f20b17979c2e1eb30c0b0a431cda045e055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Brault <adrien.brault@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:04:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the SM80 adaptive gate's packed KV fixture

Use the V4 page layout consumed by SM80 sparse decode: 448 FP8 NoPE values, 64 BF16 RoPE values, and seven 64-value scales plus padding in a separate page region. The operator gate previously wrote interleaved 528-byte V4.1 records, so its writer and reference agreed while attention read unrelated bytes.

Track the operator gate alongside CPU contract tests. Check canonical writer bytes, dense-to-ragged padding, and live/empty attention rows at both local head counts. Poison output before graph replay to detect unwritten rows. Leave serving kernels and defaults unchanged.

Origin: new
Upstream: none
---
